# A1 (QUALIFICATION): the AUDITED attach of c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full-audit (ship-full plus the verify audits and the gate marker; Lever N and packed prefix reuse ON, chunked prefill on).
# READ: ZERO audit mismatches (T1, T2, extent); '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed' at 262144 with NO UNQUALIFIED and NO evidence-waiver line; the Lever N
# route ledger clean (every chunk on a 2048 boundary, no foreign route, no final-hold fault line); prefix engaged ('[PINDIAG] prefix: install' and 'sticky admit'
# lines present); no program compiled after the warm. HASHES: concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal must be byte-equal to W1's
# reference hashes from W1's control attach (same prompts), per user: Lever N and prefix are exact or this FAILS.
# levern_equal, levern_equal_busy and levern_equal_long are NOT run here: they compare Lever N against a separate control run (A0c), which this lean pack
# drops; the W1 hash equality above is the exactness claim, and F1 runs levern_equal_busy under the fault. Real time: attach 18 + tests ~22.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-full pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of ship/262k-full (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
